Specifically:

  css/rux.css and css/rux.min.css are compiled from @carbon/styles.
    The class and custom-property prefix is changed from `cds` to `rux`
    at build time, the component set is reduced, and two of four themes
    are kept. The rules themselves are Carbon's.

  css/base/ carries the same origin.

  assets/icons.svg is assembled by tools/build-icons.mjs from individual SVG
    sources in two packages, and from drawings made here.
      `i-` path data is IBM's, from @carbon/icons.
      `m-` path data is Google's, from @material-symbols/svg-400, which is
        Material Symbols, Copyright Google LLC, under the same Apache
        License, Version 2.0.
      `r-` is drawn in assets/icons-rux/ and is ours.
    The sprite wrapper and the symbol naming are not either publisher's.

  data/carbon-*.json and data/material-glyphs.json are captures of each
    publisher's own drawings, kept as a reference for the gate that asks
    whether the sprite is faithful. They are recorded observations of the
    upstream work.

Carbon's Sass sources carry `// Copyright IBM Corp.` headers which Sass
strips when compiling, so the built CSS in this repository cannot carry
them inline. This file, and the banner tools/build.mjs writes at the top
of the built stylesheet, are where that attribution is retained instead.

